1538:## 23. The year's festivals, and the trip's dates
12:- `23.1` A full-width timeline of the coming year, one bar per festival edition, today marked and the trip's dates banded across it.
26:- `23.2` Choosing a festival on the timeline sets the trip's dates to its run plus a day either side.
39:- `23.4` A festival joins the pool only when its city is within reach of the festival that leads the trip.
51:- `23.5` A festival left out for being out of reach is named on the page, never dropped silently.
55:- `23.6` Below the site header, the page takes the theme of the festival that leads the trip: its name and its palette.
66:- `23.7` The Edinburgh Fringe is a festival like the others: chosen on the timeline, it plans its own programme in its own theme.
80:- `23.8` The trip's first and last day are set on the timeline: drag either end of the band, or type the dates, and the calendar follows.
